# Error handling rules

- Distinguish validation, explicit confirmation, domain conflict, cancellation,
  storage failure, and unexpected failure; do not flatten them into “failed.”
- User messages are concise, localized, actionable, and free of stack traces,
  SQL, raw Electron errors, backup internals, or unintended paths.
- Duplicate, overpayment, opening-balance, restore, and permanent-delete gates
  use stable machine-recognizable error/confirmation contracts plus localized
  display text.
- A confirmation authorizes the named exception only; it never weakens future
  validation or silently changes financial classification.
- Clear busy state in `finally`, prevent double submit, preserve form values
  after recoverable failure, and expose success/warning/error through accessible
  status semantics.
- Roll back failed transactions and do not commit pending attachments.
- Preserve causal context internally without logging restaurant content,
  secrets, or private file data.
